### Did Donald Trump or his campaign present any verified legal evidence in court prior to or immediately after October 30, 2020, proving that "phony ballots" were being systematically sent in to influence the 2020 United States presidential election?
Answer: Prior to October 30, 2020, the Trump campaign failed to present any verified legal evidence of systematic mail-in ballot fraud in court. When ordered by a federal judge in Pennsylvania to produce evidence of the prevalence of mail-in and dropbox fraud, the campaign "failed to produce any evidence of vote-by-mail fraud" and "offered no evidence of fraud specifically linked to dropboxes or mail-in ballots." Instead, the campaign's court filing consisted of a "paltry" collection of news articles regarding unrelated past election infractions and public records requests.

